course: dictionary
lesson: 3939
title: Names with capital letters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of one special person, place or thing. These are called proper nouns, and they always start with a capital letter. «Mount Fuji» is the name of one mountain, so both words start with capitals.
explain: The same word can also be used for a kind of thing. Fuji is also a sweet, crunchy apple. To find out which meaning is right, look at the words around it. «The climbers reached the snowy top of Fuji before sunrise» tells you it is a mountain. «She bit into a crisp Fuji at lunch» tells you it is an apple.
explain: Ask yourself two questions: Is this word naming one particular thing? Do the words around it tell me what kind of thing it is? If you can answer both, you have found the meaning.
fact: A proper noun names one particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Fuji, or Mount Fuji, is the tallest mountain in Japan, a volcano with a snowy top near Tokyo.
fact: A Fuji is a kind of sweet, crunchy apple first grown in Japan.
fact: Mount Fuji is about 3,776 metres high and last erupted in 1707.
fact: The Japanese artist Hokusai showed Mount Fuji in the distance of his print «The Great Wave off Kanagawa».
exercise: «The climbers reached the snowy top of Fuji before sunrise.» What is Fuji here? | *A mountain | A camera company | A Japanese artist | A kind of crunchy apple
exercise: «She bit into a crisp Fuji at lunch.» What is Fuji here? | A famous print | *A kind of sweet, crunchy apple | A volcano near Tokyo | A river in the north
exercise: Why does Mount Fuji start with capital letters? | Every word in a sentence starts with a capital | *It is the name of one particular mountain | It is always written in capitals on maps | It is the first word of a question
test: Which word is a proper noun, a name that starts with a capital letter? | snow | apple | volcano | *Japan
test: In «Some Fuji apples are sold in the shop», what does Fuji mean? | A famous print | A mountain in Japan | A Japanese artist | *A kind of sweet, crunchy apple
exam: Hokusai's print shows «Mount Fuji» in the distance. What kind of word is Mount Fuji? | A verb, an action word | *A proper noun, a name with capitals | A common noun for an ordinary thing | An adjective, a describing word
